# Cursor rules for this repo (Prem Bhakti app)

Read AGENTS.md at the repo root before any task — it has all project rules:
directories to skip, working rules (no commit/deploy unless asked, never print secrets),
Cloudflare Workers deploy (`node wr.mjs deploy`, never `wrangler logout`),
Firebase cost rules, Hindi/UTF-8 file safety, and the B2 upload patterns.

For codebase questions, run `graphify query "<question>"` first (graphify-out/graph.json).

Skills live in .agents/skills/ (Cursor, Codex, Antigravity and Gemini read them; Claude Code gets links
in .claude/skills/). AGENTS.md → "Agent Skills" says which to use for which task; start UI work with
prem-bhakti-ui and finish with verification-before-completion / prem-bhakti-ship.

## Design System Generator skill
When the user asks to create a design system, generate a color palette, build a theme,
create UI tokens, or set up brand styles, follow:
  .cursor/skills/design-system-generator/SKILL.md
(references/ and templates/ are next to that file)

5 phases in order — confirm with the user between phases:
1. Brand input  2. OKLCH color palettes  3. W3C tokens + CSS custom properties
4. Component CSS  5. Preview HTML page

Key rules: OKLCH colors only; components use only var(--token); Light + Dark via
light-dark() + [data-theme]; WCAG 2.2 AA contrast; output to design-system/.
